{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1563431-guildbook-monitors-\u2014-new-on-storytellers-vault","id":1563431,"title":"Guildbook: Monitors \u2014 new on Storytellers Vault","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-24T14:05:10-07:00","id":1563431,"title":"Guildbook: Monitors \u2014 new on Storytellers Vault","content":"I\u2019m happy to announce a new contribution to the Storytellers Vault: <b>Guildbook: Monitors</b>, a 74-page sourcebook for <i>Wraith: The Oblivion</i>.<br /> <br /> The Monitors were one of the original Guilds, but unlike many of their fellows they never received a Guildbook of their own. I wanted to see whether it was possible to make something resembling the missing book \u2014 developing what was already established about the Monitors rather than reinventing them.<br /> <br /> The project draws on Monitor and Lifeweb material from across <i>Wraith</i>, including the original editions, <i>The Great War</i> and Wraith20. The aim was to turn those scattered references into a playable Guild culture: how Monitors are recruited and trained, how they conduct investigations, keep archives, take commissions, work with one another, and deal with clients, the Hierarchy and the other Guilds.<br /> <br /> The central idea that emerged while working on it was that <b>the Monitors aren\u2019t really a Guild about Lifeweb. They\u2019re a Guild about Fetters.</b><br /> <br /> Lifeweb is their professional tool. What Monitors actually spend their existence studying are the connections behind Fetters, between wraiths and people, places, memories, obligations and identities, and what happens when someone becomes professionally skilled at observing, recording, protecting and manipulating those connections.<br /> <br /> The book includes the Guild\u2019s history from Stygia through the Breaking, the Mentors, Marmarans, Spinners and Tsuchigumo, everyday Monitor practice, relations with other factions, and an appendix of reports, case material, investigations and character material for use in play.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/580453/guildbook-monitors?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Guildbook: Monitors on Storytellers Vault</a><br /> <br /> I\u2019d be very interested to hear what longtime <i>Wraith</i> players think \u2014 particularly whether it feels like the Monitors could always have worked this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}